A curated, provenance-cited harness for agentic software engineering: skills, guards, a
review panel, rubrics, and multi-model routing, installed into a consuming repository by
install.sh.


Provenance
----------

This harness curates practices, prompts and rubrics drawn from published sources.
PROVENANCE.md is the authoritative attribution record for that CONTENT; this NOTICE covers
the code. Where a skill, rubric or adapter is adapted from an externally published work,
PROVENANCE.md names the source, and that work's own terms continue to apply to it. The
Apache-2.0 grant here covers our own contribution.


Components
----------

The harness is predominantly shell and markdown with no bundled runtime dependencies.
Adapters shell out to third-party CLIs (model providers, git, gh) which the user installs
themselves and which are not redistributed here.

Because this repository is Apache-2.0 and the AIOS server is AGPL-3.0-only, nothing here
may depend on that server's code. See LICENSING.md.
